DESCRIPTION >
    - `projectDocReadinessChecks` holds the per-check afdocs results behind a project's AI documentation readiness score, replicated from Postgres via Sequin.
    - One row per `projectId` + `checkId`; `projectId` joins to `insightsProjects`.id and to `projectDocReadiness`.projectId.
    - `category` is the scoring category of the check; `status` is one of pass, warn, fail, skip, error; `message` is the human-readable result; `durationMs` is not populated yet and is always NULL.
    - `details` is the raw afdocs detail JSON as a string, cut at 32 KB in Postgres, so it may not parse as JSON; extract values with string functions.
    - Postgres deletes and re-inserts a project's checks on every scoring and those deletes are not applied here, so checks dropped by a later scoring stay in this datasource.
    - Reader rule: read with FINAL and keep only the rows whose `scoredAt` equals the max `scoredAt` of that `projectId`; every row of one scoring shares the same `scoredAt`.
    - Postgres also clears a project's checks when a run fails on a different docs URL or with none, and a scoring can return no checks; show checks only when the project has an `ok` run in `projectDocReadiness`, the max `scoredAt` equals the `updatedAt` of its newest `ok` run, every run since that run has the same normalized `docsUrl` (`https://` added when no scheme, lowercase host, no `#fragment`, no trailing `/` except on the root path), and the latest `error` is not `no-docs-url` or `repo-only`. The gate is approximate when a project is scored more than once on one `runDate`, because `projectDocReadiness` keeps one row per project per day.

TAGS "Project metadata"

SCHEMA >
    `projectId` String `json:$.record.projectId`,
    `checkId` String `json:$.record.checkId`,
    `category` String `json:$.record.category`,
    `status` String `json:$.record.status`,
    `message` String `json:$.record.message` DEFAULT '',
    `details` String `json:$.record.details` DEFAULT '',
    `durationMs` Nullable(Int32) `json:$.record.durationMs`,
    `scoredAt` DateTime64(3) `json:$.record.scoredAt`,
    `createdAt` DateTime64(3) `json:$.record.createdAt`,
    `updatedAt` DateTime64(3) `json:$.record.updatedAt`

ENGINE ReplacingMergeTree
ENGINE_PARTITION_KEY tuple()
ENGINE_SORTING_KEY projectId, checkId
ENGINE_VER updatedAt
